WHY HALT ANYWAY, WITH THE PROCESS ALREADY STOPPED. The serving image carries
no HALT and `PMUS_SPRING_LIVE` / `PMUS_SPRING_ARM` are still set on the
service. The process is gone, but a redeploy or a manual restart is not, and
the standing discipline is that a money-moving bounded session does NOT
automatically repeat after a completed or expired probe. Halting is always the
fail-closed direction, and it costs nothing here because there is nothing
authorized to run.

RE-ARMING REQUIRES A NEW OWNER AUTHORIZATION. The expired mandate cannot be
extended, refreshed or reinterpreted: a new authorization means a new
`live_mandate.json` with its own `authorization_id`, `authorized_at` and
`expiry`, committed by a human, and the removal of this file in the same
reviewed change. Nothing in a session, a restart, a settlement or an
`advance_gate` may do either.

Nothing here clears a latch, restarts R1 or revives the retired rung program.
